# The Library
# Source: Myst (1993) render, reference/myst/r04-c08.png; reframed with:
#   pnpm grid reference/myst/r04-c08.png --crop 0,0,544,333 --name myst-r04-c08
# Method: translated by eye. Kept: the pale sky, the library with its pediment, portico columns
#   and door, the water tower on its tan rock, the planetarium dome, the far sea and rock arch,
#   the pines on both sides with their red trunks, the four freestanding columns, the lamp
#   stands, the lit and shadowed lawn with the columns' long shadows, the round stepped platform
#   with its drum and stair flight, the marker-switch box on its granite pedestal, the two rope
#   posts. Dropped: the brick crates behind the library, the small box at the right edge, marble
#   veining, granite grain (a few flecks only), the grass texture. Moved: nothing.
# Colours: sky → lightcyan, sea → cyan with blue dashes, marble columns and stone → lightgrey /
#   darkgrey / white, library → lightgrey with a darkgrey portico, door → brown with red panels,
#   tan rock → yellow with brown folds (pale and far, so yellow rather than the roster's brown
#   hillside body), dome → cyan with lightcyan ribs, pines → green with black shade and red
#   trunks, lawn → green, sunlit lawn → lightgreen, cast shadows → black, switch box → brown
#   panel, yellow studded border, cyan lever, darkgrey granite.
scene "The Library"
variants day

# ---------- sky ----------
# Painted first, so everything else stands on it, but held back with delay: over the original
# the viewer paints it last, filling in behind what's already there.
delay {
  color lightcyan
  rect 0, 0, 159, 167
}

